    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> entity defined in this header, bound to the clinics appointment table.</para>
<para>A thin concrete specialisation of <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref>: it fixes TABLENAME and ORGNAME and forwards the two permission-query requests to the shared base implementations. <simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref></para>
</simplesect>
A minimal <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> specialisation fixing only TABLENAME and exposing <ref refid="classClinicAppointment_1a152526d304bed176515509bd5f950144" kindref="member">getTableName()</ref>; it does not define an organisation name or the static permission-query helpers found in the other appointment specialisations. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The class name collides with <ref refid="classClinicAppointment" kindref="compound">ClinicAppointment</ref> in <ref refid="clinic_8hpp" kindref="compound">entities/appointments/clinic.hpp</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
